          "user_rubrik": "How can I cure the pain in the front of my finger considering I hurt myself while climbing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Warming up with easy climbing\u2014such as 8\u201312 easy boulder problems or 3\u20134 easy routes\u2014is effective for preparing your fingers and reducing injury risk, especially when combined with an aerobic approach hike and dynamic stretching [DOC-3]. However, using resistance bands or grip trainers before finger-intensive climbs can provide additional targeted warm-up and is recommended by many experts, particularly if you plan to attempt crimpy or hard routes [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-4]. Signs that you may be pushing your fingers too far during warm-up include sharp or acute pain, a 'tweak' sensation, persistent discomfort, or swelling. If you experience any of these, it's best to stop, avoid hard crimping, and give your fingers time to recover [DOC-1][DOC-2]. Would you like recommendations for specific grip trainers or resistance bands?",
