          "text": "For an A2 pulley strain\u2014very common in outdoor climbers with your history\u2014expect the following recovery timeline and milestones before returning to climbing:\n\n**Recovery Timeline**\n- **Mild (Grade 1):** 2\u20134 weeks for pain-free function; gentle range-of-motion exercises can start immediately. No immobilization needed.\n- **Moderate (Grade 2):** 3\u20136 weeks; brief immobilization (1\u20132 weeks), then gradual movement. H-taping is recommended for up to 3 months when climbing.\n- **Severe (Grade 3):** 6\u201312+ weeks; longer immobilization and medical follow-up required.\n\n**Return-to-Climbing Criteria**\n- No pain with daily activities or gentle finger loading.\n- Full, pain-free range of motion.\n- Ability to press or hang lightly on the finger without discomfort.\n- No swelling or tenderness at the pulley.\n\n**Key Signs to Wait For**\n- Absence of pain during gentle crimping simulation.\n- No swelling or \u201ccatching\u201d sensation.\n- Confidence in finger strength and",
