          "user_rubrik": "How should I tape my fingers after my climbing injury at the front of my finger?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "You should begin finger strengthening only after you have full, pain-free range of motion and daily activities no longer cause discomfort\u2014typically 2\u20134 weeks for mild A2 pulley strains, longer for moderate injuries. Start with mobility and endurance (not strength) as soon as pain allows, then progress cautiously.\n\n**Safe Progression Framework:**\n- **Phase 1: Mobility & Endurance**  \n  - Begin gentle range-of-motion and light resistance (e.g., rice bucket, putty, rubber band exercises) as soon as pain subsides.\n  - Focus on high reps, low resistance\u2014avoid any pain or \u201ccatching\u201d sensations.\n- **Phase 2: Gradual Strengthening**  \n  - Once you can perform Phase 1 exercises pain-free for several days, add light manual resistance or deloaded hangs (using assistance to reduce load).\n  - Progress slowly; increase resistance only if there\u2019s no pain during or after exercise.\n- **Phase 3: Climbing-Specific Loading**  \n  - Return to easy climbing with H-taping and avoid full cr",
