          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it, cheers. What are the risks if I continue climbing and don\u2019t rest with my injury at the front of my finger?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the risk if I continue climbing and don\u2019t rest with my injury at the front of my finger?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "If you continue climbing with an injury at the front of your finger, you risk extending the amount of time needed to heal. You also introduce the chance of more skin injury to the already soft, damaged, and exposed tissue. This can lead to further damage and potentially cause chronic disability, finger deformity, or even infection. It's essential to prioritize rest and proper treatment to ensure a safe and effective recovery. Continuing to climb can worsen the injury and lead to long-term consequences, so it's crucial to take a break and allow your finger to heal.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.   (",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0006-32-19661:3": 3.549814224243164,
            "clueweb22-en0008-49-08589:8": 2.3387744426727295,
            "clueweb22-en0034-45-17732:4": 2.2016074657440186,
