        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense. I definitely want to avoid any long-term issues. Once my recovery is going well, do you have any advice for returning to climbing safely\u2014like specific exercises or ways to protect my fingers?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is some advice for when I start again climbing considering that I had a finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When returning to climbing after a finger injury, it's essential to start with gentle exercises and gradually increase the intensity. You can begin with finger stretches and strengthening exercises, such as using a hangboard or finger-strengthening device. It's also crucial to listen to your body and stop if you experience any pain. Additionally, consider using protective measures like taping techniques, splints, or supports to protect your injured finger. A physiotherapist can provide you with a personalized rehabilitation plan and advise on the best exercises and protective measures for your specific injury. They can also help you develop a gradual return-to-climbing plan to ensure a safe and effective recovery.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.   (",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0039-47-17937:5": 3.922396659851074,
            "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:11": 3.0752766132354736,
            "clueweb22-en0039-47-17937:4": 1.9664403200149536,
            "clueweb22-en0021-66-06454:12": 1.7075309753417969,
