          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "To tape your fingers after a climbing injury, especially for pulley injuries, you can use the H-taping method. This involves cutting a length of rigid athletic tape and applying it in a specific way to support the injured pulley and restrict movement. The tape should be applied to keep the tendon close to the bone, and it's essential to retape between climbs as the tape will stretch and lose its effectiveness. You can also use other taping methods, such as buddy taping or immobilization taping, depending on the severity of the injury and your personal preference. It's crucial to follow proper taping techniques to avoid further injury and promote healing.",
          "user_rubrik": "How should I tape my fingers after my climbing injury at the front of my finger?",
