      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense, thanks. If there\u2019s pain in the front of my finger when I\u2019m crimping, but I don\u2019t see any visible bowstringing, does that always mean it\u2019s not a pulley injury? Or could it be something else like a flexor tendon strain or a joint issue?",
