      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Alright. For now, what basic steps can I take at home to help with the pain in the front of my finger after a climbing session? I\u2019d like some practical tips.",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I cure the pain in the front of my finger considering I hurt myself while climbing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To alleviate pain in your finger after a climbing session, start by washing off any chalk and drying your hands thoroughly. Apply a balm or lotion to moisturize and soothe the skin. You can also try submerging your fingers in ice water for a few minutes to reduce inflammation. Additionally, gently massaging your fingers and forearms can help promote healing. It's also essential to maintain good overall health through a balanced diet to reduce inflammation. If the pain persists, consider consulting a medical professional for further guidance.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.   (",
