          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s reassuring to hear. Now, how should I tape my fingers after my climbing injury at the front of my finger? Any particular method for that area?",
          "user_rubrik": "How should I tape my fingers after my climbing injury at the front of my finger?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To tape your fingers after a climbing injury at the front of your finger, you can use the H-taping method, which provides substantial support to your pulley in keeping the tendons close to the bone. Another method is to restrict movement of the finger at the joint of the injured pulley, which can help prevent further injury. It's essential to retape between climbs or whenever you feel the tape slackening, as the tape will stretch quickly and lose its effectiveness. You can also consider buddy taping, where you tape the injured finger to an adjacent finger for added support. The key is to find a taping method that provides the right amount of support and restriction to allow your finger to heal while still allowing you to climb.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.",
