      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Alright, that makes sense. I\u2019m noticing it most in my left middle finger, especially after bouldering on colder days. Any suggestions for actually managing or curing the pain at this stage?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I cure the pain in the front of my finger considering I hurt myself while climbing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To manage your left middle finger pain, rest is crucial; cease activities that stress it (P10). Apply ice for 10-15 minutes multiple times daily to reduce pain and swelling (P3, P7, P10). Over-the-counter NSAIDs like ibuprofen can also help (P2, P7, P10). Buddy taping can provide support (P7, P19). When returning to bouldering, ensure a thorough warm-up, particularly on colder days, and progress slowly to prevent re-injury (P6, P12, P16). If pain persists, consult a doctor (P19).",
