      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Understood, I'll have to watch out for that. Once the pain subsides, do you have tips for safely starting to climb again\u2014especially for someone my age? I've picked up climbing quite late and my fingers don't recover as quickly as they used to.",
          "user_rubrik": "What is some advice for when I start again climbing considering that I had a finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To safely return to climbing, start gradually with easy routes, big holds, and short sessions, avoiding crimps and overhangs. Begin gentle re-strengthening with tools like putty or a deloaded hangboard once pain-free. Use prophylactic taping for support. For your age, prioritize thorough warm-ups, listen to your body, and don't rush recovery\u2014complete healing can take months. Consider training at 70% load for better recovery and ensure adequate protein intake.",
