      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it, that\u2019s helpful. What do you usually recommend for managing that kind of finger pain? Any home remedies or things to avoid?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I cure the pain in the front of my finger considering I hurt myself while climbing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For managing pulley strain pain, immediately rest your finger and cease climbing or any activity that stresses it, especially crimping. Apply ice (wrapped in a thin towel) for 15 minutes every hour or two, and elevate your hand to reduce swelling and pain (RICE protocol). Over-the-counter NSAIDs like ibuprofen can help with pain and inflammation short-term. Light massage may aid recovery. Avoid strenuous activities and prolonged NSAID use. H-taping can also provide support.",
