          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for that. What are the risks if I continue climbing and don\u2019t rest with my injury at the front of my finger?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the risk if I continue climbing and don\u2019t rest with my injury at the front of my finger?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "If you continue climbing without resting a pulley strain, the main risk is increased downtime, meaning it will take longer for your finger to recover. Tendons and pulleys take a significant amount of time to heal, potentially 6 weeks or more, and not resting can prolong this recovery period.",
