        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Makes sense. What\u2019s some advice for when I start climbing again, considering I had a finger injury like that?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is some advice for when I start again climbing considering that I had a finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When returning to climbing after a pulley strain, gradually reintroduce activity. Start gentle re-strengthening once your finger is pain-free, using a hangboard but avoiding crimping for at least six weeks. Begin with easy, vertical routes, focusing on large holds and good footwork, keeping sessions short. Avoid overhangs, campus boards, and tweaky crimps or pockets for several months. Use prophylactic taping. Only increase intensity if easy climbing is pain-free, and continue preventive exercises indefinitely.",
