      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Good to know. Any advice on warming up or exercises to help prevent finger injuries as I start climbing again?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is some advice for when I start again climbing considering that I had a finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To prevent future finger injuries, a thorough warm-up is key. Start with 5-10 minutes of aerobic activity to increase blood flow. Then, perform dynamic stretches for fingers, wrists, and shoulders, like finger rolls or full/flat fist exercises, to improve mobility and activate muscles. Follow with 10-20 minutes of easy, sport-specific climbing on large holds, gradually increasing difficulty.\n\nFocus on proper technique: use slow, precise footwork, engage your core, and avoid intense dynamic moves, especially to crimps. Incorporate resistance bands or finger grippers for off-wall strengthening. Always listen to your body and stop if you feel pain. Static stretching is best for rest days or after climbing.",
          "citations": {
