    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great tips, thanks. About taping for pulley injuries\u2014what\u2019s the best way to apply tape to the front of my finger for support?",
          "user_rubrik": "How should I tape my fingers after my climbing injury at the front of my finger?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For pulley injuries, H-taping is recommended as it's shown to be very effective for support. To apply: Cut a 10cm x 1.5cm piece of rigid athletic tape. Cut it lengthwise from both ends, leaving a 1cm bridge. Place the bridge on the inside (palmar side) of your injured finger, on the crease of the joint above the injured pulley. Flex your finger 60\u00b0 at the joint. Wrap the upper tape bit in a ring, then the other ring below the joint. Remember to retape between each route as tape stretches.",
          "citations": {
