        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m actually trying to learn about finger injuries\u2014how do I tell them apart from each other?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I distinguish different finger injuries?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For climbers, pulley injuries often present with a \"loud pop,\" significant swelling, pain at the base of the finger, and sometimes \"bowstringing\" (bulging). To distinguish a sprain from a fracture, sprains involve ligament damage, causing inability to pick up objects or muscle cramps, while fractures are direct bone injuries. Flexor tendon ruptures lead to an inability to bend the finger, pain, or numbness. Dislocations make the finger appear crooked or out of place.",
