          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That sounds like what I might be dealing with. How can I make the pain go away and get back to climbing?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I cure the pain in the front of my finger considering I hurt myself while climbing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To alleviate pain and return to climbing, first, immediately cease all climbing and stressful activities. Apply ice, compression, and elevate your hand. Seek a diagnosis from a climbing-knowledgeable physician. Once pain and swelling subside (1-4 weeks), begin active healing with gentle range-of-motion exercises and squeezing putty. Gradually return to climbing on easy routes with big holds and short sessions. Consider prophylactic taping and avoid overhangs or campus boards initially.",
